1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,698
Flying would be freezing.

2
00:00:01,718 --> 00:00:03,804
Air cools by about 6.5 degrees

3
00:00:03,804 --> 00:00:05,298
Celsius for every kilometer

4
00:00:05,298 --> 00:00:06,438
you climb.

5
00:00:06,458 --> 00:00:07,758
So on a warm day,

6
00:00:07,778 --> 00:00:08,788
three kilometers up it's

7
00:00:08,788 --> 00:00:10,036
already around freezing.

8
00:00:10,056 --> 00:00:10,966
Add the wind:

9
00:00:10,986 --> 00:00:12,196
at minus twenty,

10
00:00:12,216 --> 00:00:14,606
flying at 100 km/h,

11
00:00:14,626 --> 00:00:16,602
it feels like minus forty.

12
00:00:16,622 --> 00:00:18,166
Exposed skin can get frostbite

13
00:00:18,166 --> 00:00:19,261
in around ten minutes.

14
00:00:20,262 --> 00:00:21,533
Climb fast and your ears

15
00:00:21,533 --> 00:00:22,667
start to hurt.

16
00:00:22,687 --> 00:00:23,651
Air trapped behind your

17
00:00:23,651 --> 00:00:24,820
eardrums can't keep up with

18
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:25,837
the pressure change,

19
00:00:25,857 --> 00:00:27,007
just like on a plane,

20
00:00:27,027 --> 00:00:27,885
only faster.

21
00:00:27,905 --> 00:00:29,013
Swallow, yawn,

22
00:00:29,013 --> 00:00:31,699
and wait for that satisfying pop.

23
00:00:31,719 --> 00:00:32,737
And clouds?

24
00:00:32,757 --> 00:00:34,357
They look like cotton candy,

25
00:00:34,377 --> 00:00:35,489
but they're made of billions

26
00:00:35,489 --> 00:00:36,839
of tiny water droplets.

27
00:00:36,859 --> 00:00:37,875
Fly through one and you

28
00:00:37,875 --> 00:00:38,815
come out soaked.

29
00:00:38,835 --> 00:00:39,595
In the cold,

30
00:00:39,615 --> 00:00:40,965
those droplets can freeze onto

31
00:00:40,965 --> 00:00:42,104
you as ice.

32
00:00:42,124 --> 00:00:43,551
Subscribe for more what ifs!
